      "message": "Hi @quic_cqiang@quicinc.com,\n\ndue to the system action bar shown in the Settings page. The setupEdgeToEdge API used in the Settings page is different with yours (see the following code snippets). So I suggest that you move your API to the WifiUtils.java to avoid the conflict problem.\n\n\n    public static void setupEdgeToEdge(@NonNull FragmentActivity activity) {\n        ViewCompat.setOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(activity.findViewById(android.R.id.content),\n                (v, windowInsets) -\u003e {\n                    Insets insets \u003d windowInsets.getInsets(\n                            WindowInsetsCompat.Type.systemBars() | WindowInsetsCompat.Type.ime());\n                    int statusBarHeight \u003d activity.getWindow().getDecorView().getRootWindowInsets()\n                            .getInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.statusBars()).top;\n                    // Apply the insets paddings to the view.\n                    v.setPadding(insets.left, statusBarHeight, insets.right, insets.bottom);\n\n                    // Return CONSUMED if you don\u0027t want the window insets to keep being\n                    // passed down to descendant views.\n                    return WindowInsetsCompat.CONSUMED;\n                });\n    }",
